# DRAW keymap preset: GIMP  (SAFEST — only DRAW-free target keys remapped)
#
# Format: actionId keycode requireMods forbidMods [device button]
#   mods bits: 1=Ctrl 2=Shift 4=Alt.  Action ids: GUI/COMMAND.BM (CMD_init) / SHORTCUTS.md.
# Policy (Rick, "safest"): applied ONLY if the target key is UNBOUND in DRAW. Collisions
# are documented, not applied — decide them in PLANS/PRESETS-KEYMAP-DECISIONS.md.
#
# GIMP's default tool letters diverge sharply from a pixel editor (P=paintbrush,
# N=pencil, K=ink, U=fuzzy-select, F=free-select, B=paths…), so most map to DRAW
# tools already on OTHER letters — these are remaps, not matches, and all collide.

# --- Safe remaps (target key free in DRAW: Ctrl+I/J/K/U/W) ---
# GIMP has no distinctive Ctrl+I/J/K/U/W layer op that DRAW mirrors 1:1 — none are
# provably safe without a decision. (none)

# --- COLLISIONS (need a decision; NOT applied) -------------------------------
#   N   Pencil              -> DRAW N is free but pencil == DRAW Dot (D); remap D->N?
#   P   Paintbrush          -> DRAW P is Polygon; GIMP paintbrush == DRAW Brush (B)
#   U   Fuzzy Select (wand) -> DRAW U free-ish; DRAW wand is W
#   F   Free Select (lasso) -> DRAW F is Fill
#   B   Paths (bezier)      -> DRAW B is Brush; DRAW bezier is Q
#   R   Rectangle Select    -> DRAW R is Rectangle DRAW tool (not select)
#   E   Ellipse Select      -> DRAW E is Eraser
#   T   Text                -> DRAW T is Text (match)
#   Shift+B Bucket Fill     -> DRAW Fill is F
#   Ctrl+, Preferences      -> DRAW Ctrl+, is Settings (match)
